# Demo requests. Run them from Visual Studio, Rider, or VS Code (REST Client extension).
# Watch the console of the running app while you send them: every step is logged.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5200

### What's in stock? (MUG: plenty, PLUSH: only 3, BOOK: none)
GET {{baseUrl}}/inventory

### 1. Happy path: reserve stock -> charge card -> order Completed
# @name happyOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "alice",
  "paymentMethod": "card-ok",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "MUG", "quantity": 2 },
    { "sku": "PLUSH", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### Ask the saga where the order is (request/response answered by the saga itself)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{happyOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}

### 2. Retry: the payment gateway fails twice, then succeeds. Watch the attempts in the log.
# @name flakyOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "bob",
  "paymentMethod": "card-flaky",
  "lines": [ { "sku": "MUG", "quantity": 1 } ]
}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{flakyOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}

### 3. Compensation: the card is declined, so the saga releases the reserved stock
# @name declinedOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "carol",
  "paymentMethod": "card-declined",
  "lines": [ { "sku": "PLUSH", "quantity": 2 } ]
}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{declinedOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}

### 4. Fault: the gateway is down. 5 attempts, then the message moves to the
###    "charge-payment_error" queue, and the saga handles Fault<ChargePayment> by releasing the stock.
# @name faultedOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "dave",
  "paymentMethod": "gateway-down",
  "lines": [ { "sku": "MUG", "quantity": 3 } ]
}

### (wait ~6 seconds for the retries to run out)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{faultedOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}

### 5. Out of stock: nothing is reserved, so there's nothing to compensate
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "erin",
  "paymentMethod": "card-ok",
  "lines": [ { "sku": "BOOK", "quantity": 1 } ]
}

### 6. Rejected by the consumer: the API gets an OrderRejected response (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "erin",
  "paymentMethod": "card-ok",
  "lines": [ { "sku": "LAPTOP", "quantity": 1 } ]
}

### 7. Bus outbox: save the stock change and publish InventoryRestocked in ONE transaction.
###    Try it with RabbitMQ stopped (docker compose stop rabbitmq): you still get a 200,
###    and the event waits in the OutboxMessage table until RabbitMQ is back.
POST {{baseUrl}}/inventory/BOOK/restock
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 5
}

### Unknown order: the saga answers OrderNotFound (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### Everything MassTransit built: queues, bindings, and each endpoint's middleware pipeline
GET {{baseUrl}}/debug/bus

### Is the bus connected to RabbitMQ?
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
